---
import Base from '@/layouts/Base.astro';
import Icon from '@/components/Icon.astro';
---

<Base title="About Me" description="Senior Software Engineer and Backend Architect specializing in high-availability systems, Drupal 11, WordPress, and DevOps.">
  <article class="flex flex-col w-full gap-8 md:gap-10">
    <header class="glass-card rounded-xl p-8 border-b-[3px] border-b-hud-cyan relative overflow-hidden group">
      <h1 class="font-display text-slate-100 text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold leading-tight tracking-tight mb-4 flex items-center gap-4">
        <div class="flex items-center justify-center w-12 h-12 md:w-14 md:h-14 rounded-lg bg-hud-cyan/10 border border-hud-cyan/20 text-hud-cyan shrink-0">
          <Icon name="account_circle" class="text-3xl md:text-4xl" />
        </div>
        About Me
      </h1>
    </header>

    <div class="glass-card rounded-xl p-8 md:p-12 prose prose-slate prose-invert max-w-none w-full prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:tracking-tight prose-a:text-hud-cyan hover:prose-a:text-cyan-400 prose-img:rounded-xl prose-h2:text-3xl prose-h2:md:text-4xl prose-h2:leading-tight prose-h3:text-xl prose-h3:leading-tight">
      <h2>Senior Software Engineer | Backend Architect | DevOps &amp; Platform Engineering | Drupal &amp; WordPress Expert</h2>

      <p>Hello, I'm <strong>Juan José Gómez López</strong>. I am a Senior Software Engineer and Backend Architect based in <strong>Cuernavaca, Mexico</strong>, dedicated to designing, scaling, and optimizing complex enterprise web platforms for global organizations.</p>

      <p>Welcome to my personal slice of the web (which, keeping things fast and lightweight, is built statically with <a href="https://gohugo.io/">Hugo</a>).</p>

      <h3>Building for Scale and Resilience</h3>

      <p>With over <strong>9 years of full-stack development experience</strong>, my career has been defined by turning intricate business requirements into high-availability digital infrastructures. I specialize deeply in the PHP ecosystem, particularly in architecting enterprise solutions using <strong>Drupal (versions 7 through 11)</strong> and <strong>WordPress</strong>.</p>

      <p>I have a proven track record of designing multisite architectures and high-availability systems. Whether it's executing <strong>zero-downtime migrations</strong> for tens of thousands of users, or building complex synchronization systems that process massive transactional queues, my goal is always to deliver secure, scalable, and resilient platforms.</p>

      <h3>The Engineering Philosophy: From Enterprise to Micro-Frameworks</h3>

      <p>My background in electronics instilled in me a fundamental appreciation for how things work "under the hood." This drives my approach to software architecture: <strong>choose the right tool for the job</strong>.</p>

      <p>While my day-to-day often involves heavy-duty enterprise environments and cloud infrastructures (AWS, Acquia, Pantheon), I am equally passionate about minimalism in code. When the project calls for it, I love building with lightweight tools like <strong>FlightPHP</strong> and <strong>SQLite</strong> to create highly efficient, resource-conscious software.</p>

      <h3>DevOps, Automation, and the Future</h3>

      <p>An application is only as good as the infrastructure it runs on. A significant part of my focus is on <strong>platform engineering, system integration, and DevOps</strong>. I am continuously modernizing legacy deployment workflows, leveraging <strong>Docker</strong> and transitioning to modern self-hosted deployment platforms like <strong>Dokploy</strong> to establish true cloud-native infrastructure.</p>

      <p>Beyond traditional web architecture, I actively explore the intersection of backend engineering and <strong>AI</strong>. I regularly utilize machine learning libraries like <strong>MLX</strong> and run models like <strong>LLaMA</strong> and <strong>Qwen</strong> locally to automate tasks and accelerate my development workflows.</p>

      <h3>Let's Connect</h3>

      <p>I am always looking toward the next architectural challenge and strongly prefer collaborating with international teams in remote environments.</p>

      <p>Whether you want to discuss enterprise CMS architecture, the nuances of local LLM deployment, or just share a great cup of coffee (preferably espresso with perfectly textured micro-foam), I'd love to hear from you.</p>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:juanjose@ingomez.com">juanjose@ingomez.com</a></li>
        <li><strong>LinkedIn:</strong> <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/juaningdotdev">linkedin.com/in/juaningdotdev</a></li>
        <li><strong>GitHub:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/neurox">github.com/neurox</a></li>
      </ul>

      <hr />

      <h3>Professional Resume</h3>

      <p>For a comprehensive chronological timeline of my professional roles, technical proficiencies, and formal certifications, you can review my formal Curriculum Vitae.</p>

      <a href="/pdf/juan-gomez-cv.pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-hud-cyan hover:text-cyan-400 transition-colors font-bold no-underline group" target="_blank">
        <span class="material-symbols-outlined">&#xe873;</span>
        <span class="group-hover:underline">Download CV (PDF)</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
